Downstream patch: open the executable wrapper with O_CLOEXEC

The wrapper descriptor is inherited by the compiler and its descendants.
Link mode waits only for the direct child before renaming the wrapper into
place, so a surviving descendant (such as a reparented linker) keeps the
wrapper open for writing and an immediately following
`libtool --mode=execute` fails with ETXTBSY.

Only the link process needs this descriptor, so mark it close-on-exec.

---
diff --git a/src/logic/linkcmd/slbt_linkcmd_executable.c b/src/logic/linkcmd/slbt_linkcmd_executable.c
--- a/src/logic/linkcmd/slbt_linkcmd_executable.c
+++ b/src/logic/linkcmd/slbt_linkcmd_executable.c
@@ -129,7 +129,7 @@
 				dctx->cctx->output) < 0)
 		return SLBT_BUFFER_ERROR(dctx);
 
-	if ((fdwrap = openat(fdcwd,wrapper,O_RDWR|O_CREAT|O_TRUNC,0644)) < 0)
+	if ((fdwrap = openat(fdcwd,wrapper,O_RDWR|O_CREAT|O_TRUNC|O_CLOEXEC,0644)) < 0)
 		return SLBT_SYSTEM_ERROR(dctx,wrapper);
 
 	slbt_exec_set_fdwrapper(ectx,fdwrap);
